<link rel="stylesheet" href="~/css/character.css" asp-append-version="true" />
<section class="characters" data-characters lang="zh-Hans">
    <header class="character-intro">
        <a class="character-back" href="/Archeon"><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">← 回到 Archeon</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>← Back to Archeon</span></a>
        <p class="kd-eyebrow" lang="en">06 · Character</p>
        <h1><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">在风与日光里</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>In wind and sunlight</span></h1>
        <p class="character-lede"><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">Anna、Lia 与 Kassia。启程之前，先在她们身边坐一会儿。</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Anna, Lia and Kassia. Before they set off again, sit with them for a while.</span></p>
    </header>
    <div class="character-toolbar" data-character-toolbar>
        <nav class="character-jumps" aria-label="人物 / Characters">
            <a href="#anna" lang="en">Anna <span>01</span></a>
            <a href="#lia" lang="en">Lia <span>02</span></a>
            <a href="#kassia" lang="en">Kassia <span>03</span></a>
        </nav>
        <div class="character-language" data-language-controls role="group" aria-label="阅读语言 / Reading language" hidden>
            <button type="button" data-character-lang="zh" aria-pressed="true" lang="zh-Hans">中文</button>
            <button type="button" data-character-lang="en" aria-pressed="false" lang="en">English</button>
        </div>
    </div>
    <p class="character-time"><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">年龄以主线开始时为准，身高与体重为约值。</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Ages are given at the start of the main story; height and weight are approximate.</span></p>

    <article id="anna" class="character-profile" aria-labelledby="anna-name">
        <figure class="character-portrait">
            <img src="/images/Anna%20Freedman-protagonist.png" width="1568" height="1407" alt="Anna 穿着红夹克，金色长发在船下的日光里扬起。" data-alt-zh="Anna 穿着红夹克，金色长发在船下的日光里扬起。" data-alt-en="Anna in her red jacket, long blonde hair lifting in the sunlight beneath a ship." fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" />
            <figcaption><span>01</span> Anna Freedman</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div class="character-copy">
            <header data-reading-anchor>
                <p class="character-place"><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">Atheria · 鹰巢</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Atheria · Eyrie</span></p>
                <h2 id="anna-name" lang="en">Anna Freedman</h2>
                <p class="character-craft"><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">Gust · 飞行与制作</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Gust · Flying &amp; making</span></p>
            </header>
            <dl class="character-facts" data-reading-anchor>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">年龄</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Age</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">19 岁</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>19</span></dd></div>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">身高</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Height</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">约 168 cm</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Approx. 168 cm</span></dd></div>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">体重</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Weight</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">约 58 kg</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Approx. 58 kg</span></dd></div>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">头发</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Hair</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">金色长发</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Long blonde hair</span></dd></div>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">眼睛</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Eyes</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">蓝灰色</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Blue-grey</span></dd></div>
            </dl>
            <div class="character-prose">
                <p data-reading-anchor><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">Anna 倾听时会微微侧过头，金色长发从肩边滑下来，露出红夹克里一截白领。她的声音偏低，说得快，字却清楚；一讲到兴头上，手里拿着的小铜件也跟着转。夹克合身，肩上的金边是她自己挑的。她喜欢隔着一段泊位就能看见的红，也在意抬起胳膊时，袖子会不会牵住肩。</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Anna tilts her head to listen, and her blonde hair slips off one shoulder, revealing a glimpse of white collar beneath her red jacket. She has a low voice and speaks fast, each word clear. When a story catches her interest, she talks with her hands, turning the little brass fitting she holds. She chose the gold trim at the shoulders herself. The red has to stand out across the moorings; the sleeves have to let her raise her arms without tugging at the seams.</span></p>
                <p data-reading-anchor><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">Gust 的栗色甲板在日光里慢慢变暖，脚下有燃料电池持续的低鸣。Anna 站得稳，目光却常往舷边去：风布刚抬起来，哪根细索的响已经变了。她会把听见的位置指给同行的人，也会蹲下来，为一只握着硌手的柄重新磨出弧度。皮手套沾着油，飞行包侧袋里那半瓶山花油，开盖时仍有一点清淡的香。</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Sunlight warms Gust’s chestnut deck, and the fuel cell hums beneath Anna’s feet. She keeps her footing, but her eyes stray towards the rail. A strip of windcloth lifts; one of the thin lines has changed its note. She points it out so her companion can listen. A handle that digs into her palm can hold her attention just as long: she crouches over it, sanding the curve, then testing it in her grip. Oil has worked into her leather gloves. In a side pocket of her flight bag, half a bottle of wildflower oil gives off a faint scent when she lifts the cap.</span></p>
                <p data-reading-anchor><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">回到 Atheria，她有时还没把包放稳，就开始向母亲讲路上的事。讲得太急，漏掉一个人名，被追问了又只好退回去重说。她爱远行，也爱把某个下午讲得让桌边的人忍不住插话；笑起来可以毫无顾忌，争起一处做法也不肯轻易让步。第二天摊开材料，她还记得昨天那个没来得及试的小念头。</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Back in Atheria, Anna can be halfway into a story before her bag is down. Her mother stops her to ask who she means—she has skipped a name and must go back. She loves the journey, and she loves this part too: an afternoon told across a table, with everyone interrupting to ask or add something. Her laughter fills the room. Let the talk turn to how something should be made, though, and she can be hard to budge. The next morning, as she spreads out her materials, she is still thinking about the idea she ran out of time to try.</span></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </article>

    <article id="lia" class="character-profile" aria-labelledby="lia-name">
        <figure class="character-portrait">
            <img src="/images/Lia%20redwood.png" width="819" height="1452" alt="Lia 扎起长发，在日光照亮的木屋与草地之间回过头来。" data-alt-zh="Lia 扎起长发，在日光照亮的木屋与草地之间回过头来。" data-alt-en="Lia looks back over her shoulder, her long hair tied up, with sunlit timber houses and grass behind her." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <figcaption><span>02</span> Lia Redwood</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div class="character-copy">
            <header data-reading-anchor>
                <p class="character-place"><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">Atheria</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Atheria</span></p>
                <h2 id="lia-name" lang="en">Lia Redwood</h2>
                <p class="character-craft"><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">颜色、织面与精细小件</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Colour, cloth &amp; small mechanisms</span></p>
            </header>
            <dl class="character-facts" data-reading-anchor>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">年龄</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Age</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">14 岁</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>14</span></dd></div>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">身高</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Height</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">约 152 cm</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Approx. 152 cm</span></dd></div>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">体重</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Weight</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">约 44 kg</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Approx. 44 kg</span></dd></div>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">头发</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Hair</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">红棕色</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Auburn</span></dd></div>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">眼睛</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Eyes</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">浅绿色</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Pale green</span></dd></div>
            </dl>
            <div class="character-prose">
                <p data-reading-anchor><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">Lia 会把样布拿到门口再看。屋里的颜色到了太阳下，边缘往往另有一点亮；她捏住两角，让织面平展开，红棕色的发丝垂到脸旁，浅绿色的眼睛还追着那一小块差别。旁边的人已经说了好看，她却要等湿气散些再答。若一道接缝留得太毛，吃饭时她也可能想起来，再抱怨一句。</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Lia carries the cloth sample to the doorway. In the sunlight, a brighter shade appears along an edge that looked dull indoors. She stretches the cloth between two corners, auburn hair falling beside her face, and studies the change with pale green eyes. Someone beside her has said it looks beautiful; she wants to wait until more of the damp has dried out. A ragged seam bothers her just as much. Hours later, over a meal, she may remember it and start complaining again.</span></p>
                <p data-reading-anchor><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">小扣件在指间闭合，轻轻一嗒，她会重新开一次，试那一点阻力。簧片回得是否齐整，绷紧的细线有没有把一边拉歪，都是她肯花时间看的东西。碰到没学过的结构，她就拿给熟悉它的人看，问清楚，再试。专心时她可以盯很久，旁边一笔画歪了，也足够让她笑得暂时放下手里的东西。</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>The clasp shuts between Lia’s fingers with a small click. She opens it again, feeling for the point where it resists. She watches the spring settle back into place, then checks whether a taut thread is pulling one edge out of line. If she has never seen a mechanism before, she takes it to someone who knows it and asks them to show her. Then she tries for herself. She can stay bent over a piece for a long time—until a crooked line in the drawing beside her makes her laugh too much to keep going.</span></p>
                <p data-reading-anchor><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">Anna 讲起远方，Lia 常在她以为已经讲完的地方接着问：风究竟从哪边来，人在地上还能不能认出空中的那座山。她想自己去看，也会记得一顿不好吃的饭，和一个值得再坐一会儿的地方。碗底还剩一点甜，她明明说饱了，勺子却又刮过去；听见朋友取笑，就抬起眼，把刚才没争完的话接下去。</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Anna thinks she has finished telling the story, but Lia has questions. Which way was the wind coming from? Would she recognise the mountain from the ground, after seeing it from the air? She wants to go there herself. She remembers the smaller things too: a meal she did not like, a place where she wished they could have stayed longer. Even now, after saying she is full, she scrapes her spoon across the sweet trace left in her bowl. A friend teases her. She looks up, spoon still in hand, and picks up their argument where they left off.</span></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </article>

    <article id="kassia" class="character-profile" aria-labelledby="kassia-name">
        <figure class="character-portrait">
            <img src="/images/kassia.png" width="785" height="1484" alt="Kassia 头顶黄铜色护目镜，发丝与肩边的布料被田野上的风吹起。" data-alt-zh="Kassia 头顶黄铜色护目镜，发丝与肩边的布料被田野上的风吹起。" data-alt-en="Kassia with brass-coloured goggles above her brow, her hair and the fabric at her shoulder lifting in the wind across the fields." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <figcaption><span>03</span> Kassia Ashcroft</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div class="character-copy">
            <header data-reading-anchor>
                <p class="character-place"><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">常在各处航路交汇地停留</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Often found where routes meet</span></p>
                <h2 id="kassia-name" lang="en">Kassia Ashcroft</h2>
                <p class="character-craft"><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">Razor · 飞行</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Razor · Flying</span></p>
            </header>
            <dl class="character-facts" data-reading-anchor>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">年龄</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Age</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">21 岁</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>21</span></dd></div>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">身高</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Height</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">约 172 cm</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Approx. 172 cm</span></dd></div>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">体重</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Weight</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">约 60 kg</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Approx. 60 kg</span></dd></div>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">头发</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Hair</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">棕色</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Brown</span></dd></div>
                <div><dt><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">眼睛</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Eyes</span></dt><dd><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">棕色</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Brown</span></dd></div>
            </dl>
            <div class="character-prose">
                <p data-reading-anchor><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">风把 Kassia 的发丝吹到眼前，她抬手拨开，护目镜的铜色边框在额上闪了一下。棕色的眼睛从高处风布移到泊位，又回来看人。她喜欢让 Razor 的进场利落又漂亮，小艇的电机声比 Gust 更尖；落稳以后，若有人看见刚才那一下，她脸上的得意也用不着藏。</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Kassia sweeps the windblown hair out of her eyes; the brass rim of her goggles catches the light above her brow. Her brown eyes move from the windcloth overhead to the mooring, then back to the person beside her. She likes to make a good entrance with Razor: a clean approach, a deft last turn, the skiff’s motor singing a higher note than Gust’s. Once she has landed, she glances at whoever was watching. If they caught that last manoeuvre, her smile says she knows it was worth seeing.</span></p>
                <p data-reading-anchor><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">Anna 说风要变，她会问是哪一根索先响，站在哪里能听清。纸上的字挤了，她嫌别人写得难读；有人说她自己的字更小，她便抽过来，念得又快又清楚，念完还要问谁没听见。她记得一个判断怎样来的，也记得朋友哪回看错了。争论能从风牌边一直带到饭桌，两个人刚为航向争过，又开始争碗里究竟是太甜还是太淡。</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>When Anna says the wind is changing, Kassia wants to know which line she heard first and where to stand to hear it herself. She has much the same impatience with cramped handwriting. Someone points out that hers is smaller; she pulls the paper over and reads it aloud, rattling through the words without swallowing a syllable. Did anyone miss that? She remembers what led to a judgement, and the occasion when a friend got it wrong. She and Anna can carry a disagreement from the wind board to the table, settling a heading just in time to argue over whether the food is too sweet or too bland.</span></p>
                <p data-reading-anchor><span data-copy="zh" lang="zh-Hans">她有自己的船、朋友和下一段去向。有时 Anna 到，她已经提起包要走；有时一顿饭吃完，她还愿意坐着，听对方把话补齐。她的玩笑可能刺人，手却照样把另一碗推过去，催人趁热吃。甜食拿少了，她会再回去一趟，回来也不肯承认刚才分得太快。谁若先笑她，往往得准备好被回敬一句。</span><span data-copy="en" lang="en" hidden>Kassia has her own ship, her own friends, and plans for where she is going next. Anna may arrive to find her with her bag in hand, about to leave. Another evening, the bowls are empty and she stays at the table, waiting for Anna to finish what she was trying to say. Her jokes can sting, but she still slides a bowl within reach and tells her to eat before it cools. If she has passed the sweets around without keeping enough for herself, she goes back for more and denies any mistake. Anyone who laughs can expect a remark in return.</span></p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </article>
